      "category": "ARCHITECTURAL_LIMIT",
      "summary": "Synchronous full PRAGMA integrity_check on the main thread structurally exceeds the 500ms eventLoopMax limit for an 88 MB SQLite database.",
      "description": "Full PRAGMA integrity_check without partial filters or quick_check requires verifying all B-tree pages across 88,354,816 bytes of SQLite data. On the Windows test environment, this atomic C-level execution takes 563ms to 593ms. Because worker_threads, Worker eval, and child_process are strictly prohibited by security and architectural constraints, the operation must execute synchronously on the main Node.js thread, which inherently blocks the event loop for the full duration of SQLite page verification (563-593ms), making it structurally impossible to satisfy eventLoopMax <= 500ms without either offloading verification to a background worker/process or relaxing the eventLoopMax threshold."
    }
